      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Query Scope**\n\nI'm focusing on defining the scope of the Python file, `query_metric_window.py`. The core function will query recent data points for a specific metric over a defined time window. I'm now thinking about selecting a concrete external provider for managed metrics monitoring. Right now, I'm considering Google as a common and feasible choice.\n\n\n**Implementing the Cloud Client**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Monitoring and will integrate the `google.cloud.monitoring_v3` library. The `query_metric_window.py` file is under construction, and I'm importing the necessary modules and laying out the basic function structure. The parameters will be project ID, metric type, an end time, and a duration in minutes. I am currently focusing on building the query using the `MetricServiceClient`.\n\n\n",
